      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Lessons for multi-GPU training&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;lessons-for-multi-gpu-training&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#lessons-for-multi-gpu-training&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is the learning note when I was trying to run experiments on multiple GPUs.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Decide on batch size convention&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;decide-on-batch-size-convention&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#decide-on-batch-size-convention&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Per-GPU batch size:what you pass to your dataloader(batch_size=..)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Effective batch size : per_gpu_batch_size * num_gpus*grad_accum_steps&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;grad_accum_steps: refers to how many steps updating the gradient, in my case grad_accum_steps=1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
